module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.ReductiveBorelPairStructure
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Sites.Fpqc
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Over
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Types.Colimits
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.FunctorCategory.Basic
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.HomogeneousOrbitQuotientGeometry
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.BorelMaximalTorusConjugacy
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.ReductiveRootSubgroupParametrizations
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.ReductiveRankOneReflections

/-! # Exhaustion of parabolics by simple-root subsets

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Theorems 17.10 and 17.16, pp.354--356;
Section 21i, Proposition 21.90 and Theorem 21.91, pp.452--454.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-parabolic-simple-root-exhaustion)

The represented quotient is the fppf sheafification of the pointwise coequalizer
of projection and right multiplication. Root subsets are subsets of the actual
character-root index type, as in the recorded Borel-pair root datum.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory Limits MonoidalCategory CartesianMonoidalCategory
open scoped MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A parabolic through a split maximal torus contains a Borel through that torus.
For every such Borel, its roots are the positive roots together with exactly the
root subsystem generated by a unique subset of the simple roots. That subset is
precisely the simple roots whose negatives occur in the parabolic's tangent space.
The conjugation actions and character-root datum are those of the recorded
Borel-pair structure theorem; in particular weights are characters, not their
differentials. The base's integral independence and signed integral expansions
also give independence in the rational character space.

Source: Milne, Theorem 17.16, p.356; Theorem 17.10, pp.354--355;
Section 21i, p.452; Proposition 21.90 and Theorem 21.91, pp.453--454.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-parabolic-simple-root-exhaustion)

Proof plan, following the seven steps of the node:
1. Choose B₀ by lem-sfb-reductive-borel-pair-structure. Its left action on the
   nonempty proper quotient G/P has a scheme-theoretically fixed F-point by
   lem-sfb-solvable-proper-fixed-point. The sheafification universal property
   identifies this quotient with lem-sfb-homogeneous-orbit-quotient-geometry.
   Lift the point to g in G(F). The coset criterion on every F-algebra gives
   g⁻¹B₀g contained in P as a subgroup scheme.
2. By lem-sfb-borel-maximal-torus-conjugacy this Borel contains a maximal torus S
   of G. Both S and T are maximal in the smooth connected group P. Conjugate S
   to T by an element of P(F), obtaining the required Borel. Now fix any Borel
   B with these containments.
3. Use lem-sfb-reductive-root-subgroup-parametrizations and
   lem-sfb-maximal-torus-overgroup-root-generation: a root occurs in Lie(P)
   exactly when its root subgroup lies in P. Thus every positive root occurs.
   A representative of s_β in P conjugates U_β to U_{-β}. Conversely, if
   -β occurs, the rank-one subgroup from lem-sfb-reductive-rank-one-reflections
   and the matrix models in lem-sfb-split-rank-one-classification give a
   representative in P: u(1) times lower(-1) times u(1) is the matrix with rows
   (0,1) and (-1,0), also in characteristic two and after passage to PGL₂.
4. Set I to the simple roots whose negatives occur. Let W_I be generated by
   their reflections and W_P be the image of N_G(T)(F) intersect P(F) in W.
   Step 3 gives W_I contained in W_P. For w in W_P, apply
   lem-sfb-bruhat-simple-letter-specialization to a reduced word: closedness
   of P places a representative of every simple letter in P, hence every
   letter belongs to I. Thus W_P = W_I, including the empty word.
5. If -β occurs for a positive root β, then s_β belongs to W_I. Every generator
   of W_I acts identically modulo the rational span of I, by the reflection
   identity in lem-sfb-reductive-rank-one-reflections and coroot uniqueness in
   lem-sfb-reductive-borel-pair-structure. Hence -2β belongs to that span.
   Independence of the simple roots makes all integral coordinates outside I
   vanish. Therefore -β is in the integral span of I. This proves one inclusion.
6. Conversely, lem-sfb-root-subsystem-simple-orbits writes any root in the
   integral span of I as wα, with α in I and w in W_I. The Weyl reflections
   of lem-sfb-reductive-rank-one-reflections act on the rational root space.
   Choose a representative in P by step 4. Root-subgroup uniqueness in
   lem-sfb-reductive-root-subgroup-parametrizations identifies its conjugate
   of U_α with U_{wα}, which therefore lies in P. Apply
   lem-sfb-maximal-torus-overgroup-root-generation to get the reverse inclusion.
7. For a simple α, -α is not positive, and it belongs to the integral span of
   a subset J of the base exactly when α belongs to J, by independence.
   Thus every J giving the displayed equality is the asserted I. For no roots,
   I is empty; for P = G, I is the whole base. No characteristic restriction,
   semisimplicity or simply connectedness is used. -/
theorem parabolic_simple_root_exhaustion {F : Type u} [Field F] [IsAlgClosed F]
    (G T P : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F))))
    (hG : ReductiveTorusCentralizer.IsReductive G)
    (iT : T ⟶ G) (hT : ReductiveTorusCentralizer.IsMaximalTorus iT)
    (hsplit : ∃ r : ℕ, Nonempty (T ≅ MultiplicativeType.splitTorus F r))
    (iP : P ⟶ G) (hP : IsClosedSubgroupScheme iP.hom.hom)
    (hPsmooth : Smooth P.X.hom) (hPconnected : ConnectedSpace P.X.left)
    (jTP : T ⟶ P) (hjTP : jTP ≫ iP = iT)
    (Q : Over (Spec (.of F))) (q : G.X ⟶ Q)
    (hQproper : IsProper Q.hom)
    (hQfinite : LocallyOfFiniteType Q.hom ∧ QuasiCompact Q.hom)
    (hQsheaf : Presheaf.IsSheaf (Scheme.fppfTopology.over (Spec (.of F))) (yoneda.obj Q))
    (hquot : ∃ ηq : coequalizer (yoneda.map (fst G.X P.X))
        (yoneda.map (fst G.X P.X * (snd G.X P.X ≫ iP.hom.hom))) ⟶ yoneda.obj Q,
      coequalizer.π _ _ ≫ ηq = yoneda.map q ∧
      ∀ Z : Sheaf (Scheme.fppfTopology.over (Spec (.of F))) (Type u),
        Function.Bijective (fun f : yoneda.obj Q ⟶ Z.obj ↦ ηq ≫ f)) :
    (∃ (B : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (iB : B ⟶ G)
      (jTB : T ⟶ B) (jBP : B ⟶ P),
      IsBorelGroupScheme iB.hom.hom ∧ jTB ≫ iB = iT ∧ jBP ≫ iP = iB) ∧
    ∀ (B : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (iB : B ⟶ G)
      (jTB : T ⟶ B) (jBP : B ⟶ P),
      IsBorelGroupScheme iB.hom.hom → jTB ≫ iB = iT → jBP ≫ iP = iB →
      ∀ (_ : IsCommMonObj T.X)
        (_ : IsCommMonObj (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F))
        (aG : ModObj T.X G.X) (aB : ModObj T.X B.X) (aP : ModObj T.X P.X),
      aG.smul = (iT.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 G.X) ≫ GrpObj.conj G.X →
      aB.smul = (jTB.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 B.X) ≫ GrpObj.conj B.X →
      aP.smul = (jTP.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 P.X) ≫ GrpObj.conj P.X →
      ∀ (Φ : Finset (Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F))))
        (D : RootDatum Φ
          (Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
          (Additive (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F) ⟶ T)))
        (b : D.Base),
      D.IsReduced →
      (∀ α : Φ, D.root α = α.val) →
      (∀ (χ : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
        (ν : Additive (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F) ⟶ T)),
        ν.toMul.hom.hom ≫ χ.toMul.hom.hom =
          (𝟙 (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)) ^ (D.toLinearMap χ ν)) →
      (∀ χ : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)),
        χ ∈ Φ ↔ χ ≠ 0 ∧ @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T G aG χ.toMul ≠ ⊥) →
      (∀ α : Φ, b.IsPos α ↔
        @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T B aB α.val.toMul ≠ ⊥) →
      ∃ I : Set Φ,
        I ⊆ (b.support : Set Φ) ∧
        {α : Φ | @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T P aP α.val.toMul ≠ ⊥} =
          {α : Φ | b.IsPos α} ∪
            {α : Φ | D.root α ∈ Submodule.span ℤ (D.root '' I)} ∧
        (∀ J : Set Φ, J ⊆ (b.support : Set Φ) →
          {α : Φ | @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T P aP α.val.toMul ≠ ⊥} =
            {α : Φ | b.IsPos α} ∪
              {α : Φ | D.root α ∈ Submodule.span ℤ (D.root '' J)} → J = I) ∧
        I = {α : Φ | α ∈ b.support ∧
          @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T P aP (-α.val).toMul ≠ ⊥} := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
